🧬 Ternary Distillation: Phase 3 Plan
🧠 The Goal
Train a small, fast, efficient AI model that runs on cheap hardware (GTX 1070, Raspberry Pi, etc.) while keeping the intelligence of a much larger model.

🔥 The Two-Step Process
Step	What It Does	Tool
1. Distillation	Use a big, smart model (teacher) to train a smaller model (student).	BitDistill, OHMS-AdaptQ
2. Ternary Conversion	Convert the student model to ternary format (-1, 0, +1).	BitDistill, OHMS-AdaptQ
📊 Why Ternary?
Metric	Normal Model	Ternary Model
Memory usage	16-bit (large)	1.58-bit (10x smaller)
Speed	Slow on old hardware	5x faster
Hardware	Needs expensive GPU	Runs on old GPUs
Intelligence	High	Nearly as high
🛠️ The Tech Stack
Tool	Purpose
BitDistill	Microsoft's official distillation tool for ternary models.
OHMS-AdaptQ	Converts any model to ternary format.
DeepSeek Analyzer	Analyzes teacher models for better distillation.
🔄 The Workflow
text
1. Pick a teacher model (e.g., DeepSeek V4 Flash)
2. Use BitDistill to train a smaller student model
3. Convert the student to ternary format
4. Test on old hardware
5. Deploy as L3/L4 containers in Syntropia
